'' 'a = type( 1, 2, 3 )' IS A SEQUENCE OF FIELD STORES, the same ones the DIM
'' initialiser makes. Measured:
''
''   *(float*)&A3$0 = 0x1.8p+0f;
''   *(float*)((uint8*)&A3$0 + 4ll) = 0x1.8p-1f;
''   *(float*)((uint8*)&A3$0 + 8ll) = 0x1.2p+1f;
''
'' -- no temporary and no copy. Only the DIM position read the form, so every later
'' assignment of one declined: optimizations/vector.bas is 24 of them, now 0.
''
'' ONLY OVER A TYPE WITH NO CONSTRUCTOR, and the two are different. 'x = type<C>( )'
'' over a type that HAS one builds a temporary and memcpys it --
'' '_ZN1CC1Ev( &TMP$2$0 ); __builtin_memcpy( &X$0, &TMP$2$0, 8 )' -- and a type whose
'' fields need construction, a string member say, REJECTS the form outright: error 99,
'' "No matching overloaded function, E.constructor()".
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/typelit-assign.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/typelit-assign.out
